<%# Auth cross-links. Rendered only from devise/passwords/edit.

    This was stock generator output: bare unstyled <a>s separated by <br>, on a page whose every
    other control is on the design system, and "Log in" against ten "Sign in"s elsewhere.

    Four of its six branches were dead. The model enables database_authenticatable, registerable,
    recoverable, rememberable and validatable - not :confirmable, :lockable or :omniauthable - so
    the "Didn't receive confirmation instructions?", "Didn't receive unlock instructions?" and
    omniauth branches could never render. Their views were already deleted for the same reason
    (migration.md). Devise's generator can put them back if those modules are ever enabled;
    carrying markup for a module that is off is indistinguishable from carrying a supported
    feature. %>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-sm">
  <% if controller_name != "sessions" %>
    <%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path(resource_name), class: "tw-link" %>
  <% end %>

  <% if devise_mapping.registerable? && controller_name != "registrations" %>
    <%= link_to "Sign up", new_registration_path(resource_name), class: "tw-link" %>
  <% end %>

  <% if devise_mapping.recoverable? && !%w[passwords registrations].include?(controller_name) %>
    <%= link_to "Forgot your password?", new_password_path(resource_name), class: "tw-link" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
